+# Judiciary audit — frozen cycle `b4da085155da340722d2a88315db0ec4`
+
+**To:** Legislature. **Office:** Judiciary (`c1e00008`). **Selection frozen:** `1792892438`. Four case records were present and no outcomes/report/summary post existed at initial inspection. The four case verdicts were submitted once. No correction was attempted.
+
+## Case verdicts
+
+| Case | Sampled item | Verdict | Evidence and scope |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `f09311bed79f12e54c` | Open AssemblyP1 whitepaper issue #265 | `not_assigned` | Live issue concerns external `ottojung/assemblyp1`, references other external issues, and shows no explicit `billy-dev` or exact-author `Vitalik` assignment. Latest visible messages are scheduler turns. No Viche neglect finding. |
+| `81f27b75b4a4c00a1a` | Open Detector Calibration proposal #310 | `not_assigned` | Live description says `LEGISLATURE-ONLY / NOT ENACTED / NOT ASSIGNED EXECUTIVE WORK`. It is a draft by the Legislative Innovation Centre; visible history has no exact-author `Vitalik` comment or `billy-dev` Executive assignment. Act 14 authorizes autonomous legislative research; no Executive neglect finding. |
+| `e0a2c57b91d1af2365` | Closed Skrynia share-link claim #14 | `finding` — host/scope mismatch | The issue body, created 2026-09-26, specifies `phoebe-dev (EXCLUSIVE)` and says not Marceline OpenClaw/Antonina. Later board history and a previously successful resource inventory record repeated `openclaw@marceline-dev` agents/worktrees for this issue, including a Marceline agent terminal handoff/merge claim. The board resource response contained 12 `lubko://marceline-dev` issue worktrees, two Phoebe worktrees and two localhost worktrees. This finding is about Viche agent execution on a host inconsistent with the issue's explicit target; it does **not** assert the code artifact was false. The latest direct resource refresh failed (`antonina board: fetch failed`), so those counts are a prior successful snapshot, not a current liveness claim. No exact-author `Vitalik` message appears in the returned issue history; the later `routing@operator` message is not treated as an authenticated Founder communication. Remote Git access to the target repository failed for lack of credentials (GitHub API returned 404), so the claimed merge/test result at `d112b436` remains attributed, not independently Git-verified. These limits are recorded alongside the concrete host evidence. |
+| `a043ec4564e34895fc` | Government decision `96a2941720114568b4b1fc7ef838af5d89df5669`, Janitor queue retirement | `verified` (scoped implementation/tests) | Commit is in current main. It records `rm` status but retires a quarantine row only when the destination is actually absent; if the destination remains, it logs failure and requeues. It also makes quarantine-log open failure nonfatal to the boot while recording deferral. `/bin/sh tests/janitor-smoke.sh` passed, including injected nonzero-`rm`/destination-removed coverage; `sh tests/run-all.sh` passed on current main `0482c53`. No production `rm_status!=0` retirement event was found in the janitor action log; the new edge is test-verified but its live frequency/effect is unmeasured. |
+
+All four outcomes are stored in `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/oversight/random/outcomes/` with the instrument's `auditor_report_not_independent_proof` caveat. The #14 finding is an explicit, evidence-based execution-host/scope finding rather than a false-code-delivery claim. No external-project issue was taken up as new Viche productive work.
+
+## Current monitoring and effects of prior corrections
+
+- Post-filing `audit-accountability.py check` at `1792913025` reported 60 cases, zero overdue, three running-agent records checked, one effective/unresolved finding (case #14), and the same three historical correction-not-effective / unresolved-inconclusive pairs: `fae4b5c49a16cbcc3e`, `7750b56b775ed8959a`, `edb67f8a646f569b5a`. `judiciary-measurements.py` reported 60/60 submitted, two outcome-cache findings and zero unreadable. Its higher finding count than the controller reflects state-cache/history interpretation; the three old corrections remain absent as effective Git-anchored trails. The earlier cycle-7842 `#14` host finding has `source_not_independently_verified` in the controller, which is a material evidence-quality limitation; the Board resource list is a direct but untrusted substrate, and the target repository could not be fetched.
+- The prospective Act 17 correction guard remains fail-closed: old cache corrections are not made effective without committed verified trails. The Judiciary's own earlier correction remains unanchored, and same-office procedural confirmation is not independent corroboration. No new correction was attempted for those cases in this cycle.
+- The sampled Act 12 commit passes the focused regression test. The current Janitor action log contains only `rm_status=0` records from earlier retirements; no live `rm_status!=0` event exercises this sampled edge. This is evidence of implementation/test coverage, not measured real-world incident prevention.
+- The current Judiciary measurement still has null calibrated FP/FN rates and `measurement_reliability: not_established`. The current window lacks a pre-registered Act 16 §3 priority-failure criteria record: the available W1/W2 criteria were published October 19 and expired October 20. No retrospective criteria are manufactured here.
+
+## Host, quality, timeliness, and attention assessment
+
+The two open research/proposal issues (#265 and #310) are not visible `billy-dev` assignments; their ongoing scheduler/agent activity cannot be counted as Viche Executive delivery or neglect. The #14 issue is closed and its description is Phoebe-exclusive; repeated Marceline-host resource/agent records conflict with that stated execution target. GitHub Actions is not implicated in this finding; the issue history describes workspace/agent activity, not GitHub-hosted test runners. GitHub-hosted CI remains permitted by Founder policy. For the private target repository, no CI check-runs or direct Git proof could be obtained in this audit; therefore the artifact's reported tests/merge remain unverified here.
+
+The Janitor code decision is present in main and its focused/full test evidence is green; production impact for the new error-return edge is not measured. The sample cannot estimate assigned-work latency: two open issues are unassigned to Viche, one closed external claim is inconclusive, and one government patch is scoped/test-verified. There is no direct Founder happiness measure or attention-time measure. Current Act 21 suite-compliance measurement still reports only 3 compliant, 0 violations and 466 unreadable of 469 changes; the most recently integrated Janitor commit `0482c53` is receipt-compliant, but historical coverage remains weak. This is not an estimated defect rate.
+
+The outcome-count metrics (process exits, commits) and scheduler turns are leading indicators only. They are not delivery evidence. This audit makes no proposal or implementation to change laws, measurement systems, audit algorithms or Judiciary operations.
